'''trimester''' (trī-mes′tėr), ''n.'' [= F. ''trimestre'' = Sp. It. ''trimestre'', < L. ''trimestris'', of three months, < ''tres'' (''tri-''), three, + ''mensis'', month: see ''month.'' Cf. ''semester.''] A term or period of three months. ''Imp. Dict.''

'''trimestral''' (trī-mes′tra̤l), ''a.'' [< L. ''trimestris'' (see ''trimester'') + ''-al.''] Same as ''trimestrial.''

